# Findings we accept on purpose. Each one needs a reason; anything not listed fails CI.

# Public ALB: it has to be reachable by CloudFront. Its security group only allows
# CloudFront's IP ranges, and it rejects requests without the secret origin header.
AVD-AWS-0053

# Plain HTTP on the ALB listener: only CloudFront can reach it (see above), and
# viewers always use HTTPS. Setting alb_certificate_arn switches the origin to HTTPS.
AVD-AWS-0054

# Task egress to 0.0.0.0/0 on 443 only: ECR, Secrets Manager and CloudWatch have no
# fixed IP ranges. Postgres egress is limited to the VPC CIDR.
AVD-AWS-0104

# S3 site bucket uses SSE-S3: it holds public static assets, a customer key adds cost
# and nothing else. The state bucket and the database use their own keys.
AVD-AWS-0132

# SNS alerts topic uses the AWS-managed key: alarm messages contain no sensitive data.
AVD-AWS-0136
